    "custom_accordion_faq_6gPCJc": {
      "type": "custom-accordion-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "header_link_4ywDAJ": {
          "type": "header_link",
          "settings": {
            "link_text": "Ingredients' List",
            "link_url": "shopify://collections"
          }
        },
        "header_link_UdTx7c": {
          "type": "header_link",
          "settings": {
            "link_text": "Clinical Studies",
            "link_url": "shopify://collections/accessories"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_FWEU8m": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Superior absorption",
            "answer": "<p>Many vitamins and minerals need to be converted into a “bioactive” form before your body can use them effectively. For some people, this natural process isn’t always efficient due to genetic or metabolic differences.<br/>We use pre-activated nutrients that are already in their active forms, so your body can absorb them more readily. This supports better bioavailability - meaning more of the nutrient reaches your system in a form your body can actually use, minimising wastage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_prMn6G": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Improved effectiveness",
            "answer": "<p>When a supplement is easier to absorb, more of its beneficial compounds make it into your bloodstream and tissues. Lower-quality formulations often pass through the digestive tract with far less impact.<br/>By choosing high-absorption forms, you’re giving your body a better opportunity to achieve healthy nutrient levels and experience the intended benefits.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q8d3n7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Quicker results",
            "answer": "<p>Efficient absorption allows nutrients to begin working sooner.<br/>This can translate into earlier support for areas such as energy production, mood regulation, or hormonal balance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6m7wCF": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "No side effects",
            "answer": "<p>Nutrients that are difficult for the body to absorb can place unnecessary strain on digestion, sometimes leading to bloating, nausea, or discomfort.<br/>Our highly absorbable forms require less digestive processing making them gentler and more suitable for individuals with sensitive stomachs.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
